/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*-----------------------*\
  Membrane MODULE (CASE-LOCAL): Toray ROMEMBRA TM820E-400 seawater element,
  as the Campo de Dalias case study states it.  NOT a catalogue record: no
  Toray record is in data/standards/assets and this one implies no
  sponsorship, endorsement or data-sheet reading (DEV.md 4c C189, C194).

  SOURCE.  Toray Industries, "Seawater Desalination Using Toray's RO
  Membranes to Support a Thriving Agricultural Economy", MC-CS-CAMPODEDALIAS-1910
  (2019), Table 1, first-pass column -- a MANUFACTURER'S two-page case study;
  every performance figure is Toray's own claim "based on manufacturer's test
  conditions", not a measurement of this case.

  WHAT THE DOCUMENT STATES (origin literature):
      active area            37 m2 (400 ft2)
      flow rate              28.3 m3/d (7,500 gpd)
      NaCl rejection         99.75 %
      boron rejection        91 % at pH 8
      feed pressure          5.52 MPa (800 psi)
  WHAT IT DOES NOT STATE, and this record ASSUMES (origin assumed):
      the TEST CONDITIONS those figures belong to -- feed salinity, recovery,
      temperature, whether the 5.52 MPa is the test pressure or the plant's
      operating pressure.  READ HERE AS BOTH: the pressure of the test and
      of the plant (the document prints it beside the flow and the
      rejection, which are test figures).  The standard seawater test is
      ASSUMED: 32,000 ppm NaCl, 25 C, 8 % recovery (the conditions the
      SW30HR-380 record in the catalogue quotes from the DuPont sheet, Form
      No. 45-D00971-en, Rev. 7), the boron test at 5 ppm boron beside it
      (the same sheet).  If Toray's own differ, so do the intrinsic
      rejections derived below.
  THE GEOMETRY is not in the document either: an 8-inch x 40-inch spiral
  element, so the channel is the SW30HR-380 element's (spacer 28 mil, leaf
  length 0.95 m), carried here as an announced ESTIMATE, unverified.

  TWO RATED TESTS, one per solute, each inverted by the module's own film
  into the intrinsic rejection the `constantRejection` law needs
  (`rejection { NaCl ( fromRatedTest naclRef ); boron ( fromRatedTest boronRef ); }`).
  THE BORON PROBE is water + 5 ppm boron at the NaCl test's pressure and
  permeate flow, so it has no osmotic pressure to oppose it and runs at a
  higher recovery than 8 %: the engine prints its permeate and recovery at
  the probe beside the sheet's, and the intrinsic boron rejection derived
  from it is a constant (the law does not move it with flux or pH).  That is
  the approximation the case declares; see its flowsheetDict header.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

name           TM820E-400;
kind           membraneModule;
manufacturer   "Toray (as stated in case study MC-CS-CAMPODEDALIAS-1910; no data sheet read)";
membrane       TM820E;
format         spiralWound;

activeArea     37 m2;              // the case study, Table 1 (400 ft2)
feedSpacer     Spacer-28mil;       // ESTIMATE, see provenance
leafLength     0.95 m;             // ESTIMATE, see provenance

ratedTests
(
    {
        id                 naclRef;
        solute             NaCl;
        feedMassFraction   32.0e-3;     // ASSUMED standard seawater test (see header)
        P                  5.52 MPa;    // the document's "feed pressure"
        pressureBasis      feedGauge;   // ASSUMED: a data-sheet pressure is gauge unless it says otherwise
        T                  298.15 K;    // ASSUMED
        recovery           0.08;        // ASSUMED
        permeateFlow       28.3 m3/d;   // the document: 7,500 gpd per element
        permeateFlowBasis  sameTest;
        rejection          0.9975;      // the document: 99.75 %
        source             "Toray case study MC-CS-CAMPODEDALIAS-1910, Table 1 (rejection, flow, area, pressure: stated; salinity, recovery, temperature: assumed standard seawater test)";
    }
    {
        id                 boronRef;
        solute             boron;
        feedMassFraction   5.0e-6;      // ASSUMED: 5 ppm boron, the DuPont sheet's test (SW30HR-380 record)
        P                  5.52 MPa;
        pressureBasis      feedGauge;
        T                  298.15 K;
        pH                 8;           // the document: "91 % at pH 8"
        recovery           0.08;        // ASSUMED
        permeateFlow       28.3 m3/d;
        permeateFlowBasis  sameTest;
        rejection          0.91;        // the document: 91 %
        source             "Toray case study MC-CS-CAMPODEDALIAS-1910, Table 1 (boron rejection 91 % at pH 8 stated; boron concentration, recovery, temperature assumed)";
    }
);

provenance
{
    source  "Toray Industries case study MC-CS-CAMPODEDALIAS-1910 (2019), Table 1; a manufacturer's claim";

    leafLength
    {
        origin        estimated;
        reviewStatus  unverified;
        notes         "(the feed spacer, the 28 mil of Spacer-28mil, is carried over too, equally unverified) borrowed from the SW30HR-380 record (same 8-inch x 40-inch format, leaf length 0.95 m, itself an estimate); the document states no geometry; to be verified against the Toray element's data sheet";
    }
}
